---
/** Terms of Use. DRAFT pending legal review. Static. */
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import {staticContext} from '../../server/page';

export const prerender = true;

const {site, viewer} = await staticContext(Astro.request);
---

<Legal
  site={site}
  viewer={viewer}
  title="Terms of Use"
  path="/legal/terms"
  description="The terms for using the Conflict Intelligence Training website, community, programs and products, operated by NAMASTE International Inc. (Canada).">
  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>About these terms</h2>
    <p>
      These terms apply to the Conflict Intelligence Training website, our online community, our programs and our
      products, all operated by NAMASTE International Inc. (Canada). By using any of them, you agree to these terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Your account</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Please give accurate information when you join, and keep it up to date.</li>
      <li>You are responsible for keeping your sign-in details private and for what happens under your account.</li>
      <li>If you believe someone else has used your account, please tell us right away.</li>
      <li>To join, members must be at least <mark>[MINIMUM AGE: Ian to confirm]</mark> years old.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Using the community</h2>
    <p>
      Our community is a place to learn about conflict together. Everyone who takes part agrees to follow our
      <a href="/community/guidelines">Community Guidelines</a>. Moderators may remove posts that put someone at risk or
      break those agreements.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Confidentiality</h2>
    <p>
      What is shared in confidence stays in confidence. Please do not share outside the community what other members
      share inside it. When we share a situation from our work, we change or leave out anything that could identify the
      people involved. We cannot guarantee that every member keeps confidence, so we invite everyone to share
      thoughtfully.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>What you share</h2>
    <p>
      You keep ownership of what you post. By posting, you allow us to host and display it within the community so that
      the community can work. You are responsible for having the right to share what you post.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Our intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Seven Levels Framework, our programs, videos, live sessions, the Conflict Exploration Kit and its workbook, our
      books and the content of this website belong to NAMASTE International Inc. or to those who license them to us. They
      are for your own learning. Please do not copy, record, resell or teach them without our written permission.
    </p>
    <p>Use of our materials in professional practice: <mark>[PROFESSIONAL USE OF MATERIALS: Ian to confirm what is permitted]</mark>.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Not professional advice</h2>
    <p>
      Nothing shared on this website, in the community, in our programs or in our products is professional, legal,
      medical or counselling advice. It is an invitation to explore. For advice about your own situation, please speak
      with a qualified professional.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Not a crisis service</h2>
    <p>
      This is a learning community, not an emergency or counselling service. If you or someone you know is in danger,
      please contact your local emergency services or a crisis line in your country.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Purchases</h2>
    <p>
      Prices are shown on this website in US dollars (USD). Payments are processed by
      Stripe. Refunds and cancellations are described in our
      <a href="/legal/refunds-and-cancellations">Refunds and Cancellations</a> policy, and delivery in our
      <a href="/legal/shipping">Shipping</a> policy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Ending your membership</h2>
    <p>
      You may close your account at any time by writing to
      <a href="mailto:hello@namasteintl.com">hello@namasteintl.com</a>. We may suspend or close an account that breaks
      these terms or the Community Guidelines. When an account closes, access to the community ends.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Limits of our responsibility</h2>
    <p>
      We offer our website, community, programs and products as they are. To the extent the law allows, NAMASTE
      International Inc. is not responsible for indirect or consequential loss arising from their use. Nothing in these
      terms limits rights you have under consumer protection law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
    <p>
      When we change these terms, we update the effective date above. When a change is significant, we tell members by
      email or in the community.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the Province of <mark>[PROVINCE: Ian to confirm]</mark> and the federal laws
      of Canada that apply there. Any dispute will be heard by the courts of that province.
    </p>
  </section>
</Legal>
